6: /// <summary>
7: /// Tests that agent-plugin version resolution reads only the sources it is given (<see cref="AgentPluginVersionSources"/>):
8: /// the plugin root an environment variable names, then the plugin folder beside the workspace, then the plugin caches
9: /// under the user profile, then the synced version; and that the sources the unit-test assembly installs are hermetic
10: /// (no plugin-root variable, no sibling folder, an empty temporary profile).
11: /// </summary>
12: /// <remarks>
13: /// Requirement coverage: TR-MCP-WS-005 / FR-MCP-018 ac-1 (unit tests take every plugin-version input from
14: /// test-owned data). Found by hostile validation round 3 (finding R3-F1: the assembly fixture replaced only the
15: /// profile, so a plugin-root variable reached 19 unit tests); fix chosen by the operator on 2026-10-20 ("Structural
16: /// fix, round 4 (Recommended)"). Test data: a temporary root per test holding test-owned plugin folders with fixed
17: /// versions (environment root 4.0.0, sibling root 3.0.0, profile cache 2.0.0) and a stand-in for the machine (a
18: /// plugin-root variable at 9.0.0, the folder beside the workspace at 8.0.0, a profile cache at 7.0.0); no real
19: /// environment variable, machine folder or profile is read. Expected versions follow the criterion's reading order.
20: /// Negative controls run deliberately wrong resolutions that read one machine input instead of the given source, and
21: /// hermeticity controls reject sources that name a plugin root, compute a sibling, or point at a populated or
22: /// non-temporary profile.
23: /// </remarks>
